## CSS and Accessibility

## 1. Focus Styles

Never remove focus outlines without replacing them — keyboard users lose navigation entirely:

```css
/* Bad */
* { outline: none; }

/* Good — custom, visible focus style */
:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid #0070f3;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

`:focus-visible` only shows for keyboard navigation, not mouse clicks — best of both worlds.

## 2. Color Contrast

WCAG 2.1 AA requires:
- Normal text: **4.5:1** contrast ratio
- Large text (18px+ or 14px+ bold): **3:1**
- UI components and graphics: **3:1**

Test with: browser DevTools, axe, or Colour Contrast Analyser.

## 3. Relative Units

```css
/* Bad — ignores user's browser font-size preference */
body { font-size: 14px; }

/* Good — scales with user preference */
body { font-size: 1rem; }  /* 1rem = user's base font size */
.small { font-size: 0.875em; }
```

## 4. Visually Hidden Content

```css
.sr-only {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px; height: 1px;
  padding: 0; margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip-path: inset(50%);
  white-space: nowrap;
}
```

## 5. Motion

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

